        {
          "id": 419307876,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Do you have a link to the the GitLab issue with the sample capture? I somehow fail to find that trace.\n\nI am not sure the fix is right/complete, even if all fragments are available, a dissector might ask for even more data. These flags were added to the TCP dissector in commit ca423314373b0a4ce7d6bc1cf94c4995e1263ea2 where an additional case exists to clear the flag in case the subdissector requests more data. Is that also needed here?\n\nBTW, QUIC reassembly is still very new and is complicated by having multiple streams in a single \"Frame\" whereas TCP often has a single stream in a \"Frame\". There may be bugs or missing functionality as evidenced by the various TODO/XXX comments.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-09-27T21:53:27.831Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-09-27T21:53:27.831Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 72200690,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
