  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "b9a2d861e48bde1214de938a6b91f42e6ee2165f",
      "short_id": "b9a2d861",
      "created_at": "2020-09-28T23:07:37.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "c597927da829f9f9aab3e175347f85649e103a45"
      ],
      "title": "quic: fix reassembly issue for smb2 (and other protocols)",
      "message": "quic: fix reassembly issue for smb2 (and other protocols)\n\nIf we did not find an msp that matched the current segment we would\ntry to find the msp for set-1 instead. This will only work IFF\nwe do not know the the exact size of the PDU and where it ends,\ni.e. DESEGMENT_ONE_MORE_SEGMENT and friends.\n\nIn the case where \"get msp for seq-1\" gives us an msp where we know the exact\nPDU boundary and the current seq is beyond the end of that boundary, then\nwe should not use the msp for seq-1 but instead treat this as a brand new PDU.\n\nThis fixes issues with SMB2-over-QUIC dissection that can be seen in the\nsample capture for the \"add smb2-over-quic\" bug where only the first\nmulti-segment PDU would be dissected correctly for each direction.\n\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>\n",
      "author_name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
      "author_email": "ronniesahlberg@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2020-09-26T06:57:31.000+10:00",
      "committer_name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
      "committer_email": "ronniesahlberg@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2020-09-28T23:07:37.000+00:00",
